# Python tests

Single rule for all Python test conventions in this repo.

## Layout (mirror source)

Tests live under a top-level `tests/` directory and **mirror paths relative to the package root** — do **not** repeat the installable package folder name under `tests/`.

### Libs (`libs/backend/<pkg>/`)

```text
libs/backend/payflow_common/
  payflow_common/models/base.py
  payflow_common/models/mixins/id_model_mixin.py
  tests/models/test_base.py
  tests/models/mixins/test_id_model_mixin.py
```

Rule: `tests/<path-inside-package>/test_<module>.py`  
Not: `tests/payflow_common/models/...`

### App domain modules (`apps/backend/api/modules/<name>/`)

Same idea (ADR-0004) — mirror layers under `tests/` without an extra module-name prefix:

```text
modules/sample_module/services/hello_service.py
modules/sample_module/tests/services/test_hello_service.py
```

### Do

- One test module per source module when practical (`test_<stem>.py`)
- Keep nested folders in sync when adding new source packages
- Keep tests as a sibling of the package (`tests/`), not inside the installable tree

### Do not

- Nest `tests/<package_name>/...` when `<package_name>` is already the lib’s import root
- Dump all tests flat in `tests/` when the package has nested packages
- Keep an `apps/backend/api/tests/` tree for `core/` or app wiring — API tests live only under `modules/<name>/tests/` (ADR-0004)

## Module docstring (business use cases)

Every Python test module’s **module docstring** must list the **business use cases** covered in that file as a **bullet list** — not test function names.

```python
"""Short optional summary of the subject under test.

- Returns UUID primary key column named id
- Composes with OrmBaseModel for mapped tables
"""
```

- First line(s) may briefly name the subject (optional but preferred)
- Then one bullet per use case / behavior the file asserts, in plain language
- Prefer domain/outcome phrasing (“lists sample items from the repository”) over implementation detail (“calls list_all”)
- Keep bullets aligned with the tests in file order (one bullet per test is typical; split only when a single test covers distinct cases)
- Update the docstring whenever coverage changes

### Do not

- List `test_*` function names as the bullets
- Omit the list when the file has only one test
- Use prose paragraphs instead of bullets for the coverage list
